# =============================================================================
# batch-service/.dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build-context exclusions for the Spring Batch service (CBACT01C-CBACT04C, CBCUS01C).
#
# docker-compose.yml builds this image with `context: ./batch-service`, and the
# Dockerfile consumes exactly ONE input from that context: the repackaged Spring
# Boot fat jar under target/. Everything else - the whole src/ tree, the compiled
# classes, the surefire/failsafe reports, the *.jar.original thin jar - is dead
# weight that Docker would otherwise transfer to the daemon on every build.
#
# Before this file existed the context measured 64 MB, so each of the nine
# backend builds shipped tens of megabytes of host build output and invalidated
# its own cache whenever any unrelated file under the module changed.
#
# The allowlist form below is deliberate: a denylist has to be extended every
# time the build produces a new artifact, whereas this excludes everything and
# then re-admits only target/*.jar. `target/*.jar.original` is NOT re-admitted,
# because the `*.jar` pattern matches only names ending in `.jar`.
#
# The Dockerfile and this file are themselves excluded: BuildKit reads the
# Dockerfile through a separate channel, not from the transferred context.
# =============================================================================

# --- Exclude the entire module ----------------------------------------------
*

# --- Re-admit only the repackaged boot jar the Dockerfile copies -------------
!target
target/*
!target/*.jar
